  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_037: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) achieves 0.7062 accuracy. The only prior evidence on fusion method comes from pca_n2000, where weighted (0.6352) narrowly beat concat (0.6287) by ~0.007. However, scvi_n200 produces a fundamentally different (nonlinear, learned) representation than linear PCA, so the optimal fusion strategy may shift. Config_036 is a minimal single-variable ablation of the best config (changing only weighted→concat), directly testing whether the small fusion-method gap observed with pca_n2000 persists or reverses with scvi_n200. If concat performs comparably, fusion method is not a critical design axis and remaining budget can target higher-impact choices (e.g., aggregation method with scvi_n200). If weighted clearly wins, it confirms the current design and reduces uncertainty about the remaining search space. Under a tight budget, this clean ablation of the top configuration is the most efficient way to either confirm or challenge a key design decision before committing further experiments."
}

